0.01 2026-11-16
     - initial App::AnteREPL release, with the anterepl executable
     - added scrolling screen editing, numbered source, RUN, LIST ranges,
       slow/pause controls, undo, local EDITOR support, dump, and peek
     - LOAD accepts ordinary Perl and numbered PERL ANTE REPL files; SAVE
       preserves the loaded format and writes plain source to .pl files
     - added AUTO entry with a default increment of 5; AUTO OFF or Ctrl-C
       ends entry without losing stored lines
     - added environment inspection, literal SET/UNSET, EDIT ENV using
       VAR=value files, SAVE/LOAD/RELOAD, and startup environment RESET
     - completed built-in HELP, linked the user wiki, and added a Dist::Zilla
       configuration with an explicit list of files for the CPAN release
     - implemented the terminal integration checks in Perl using IO::Pty
     - added CLS to clear the display while retaining the stored program,
       live Perl workspace, environment, AUTO settings, and source undo
     - fixed Ctrl-C during LIST on Unix with Term::ReadKey installed
     - made AUTO entry quiet by default, with AUTO ECHO ON/OFF control;
       documented multiline immediate execution and shared subroutines
     - made Ctrl-D end AUTO without exiting, restricted the EVAL command
       to uppercase, and added Shift-Enter/Ctrl-N for inserting a newline
       into the current screen entry without submitting it
     - clarified that EVAL leaves AUTO active and function definitions are
       silent; tested session-only functions without storing their source
     - removed the experimental STORE command and pending EVAL source state
     - added FUNCTIONS to list defined workspace functions, including imports;
       documented redefinition warnings and one-time EVAL setup statements
     - made screen editing insert by default; Insert still toggles overwrite
     - rerunning an earlier screen entry replaces its previous output directly
       below it, removes stale result rows, and retains later entries
     - removed the extra blank spacer before later commands after a rerun;
       preserved deliberate blank output and the following entry's text
     - made Left at the start of a screen row move to the previous row's end,
       stopping at the first retained row
     - renamed the banner, HELP, diagnostics, and native-file header to
       PERL ANTE REPL; LOAD still accepts legacy BASIC PERL V0.1 files
     - require uppercase REPL commands and subcommands, including DUMP and
       PEEK; lowercase/mixed-case input follows ordinary Perl and AUTO rules
     - print a newline when QUIT/EXIT exits, including their forced forms;
       screen mode writes it after restoring the original terminal display
     - bound active screen memory to terminal rows and columns, with wrapped
       lines and no off-screen history; clipped entries cannot run partially
     - warn when a resize crops the screen and keep one inactive copy;
       growing adds blank space, while RECOVER explicitly restores that copy
     - make CLS forget the resize copy and HELP pause by screenful; document
       the screen, numbered source, and live workspace as separate state
     - replace command-like bareword errors with uppercase spelling hints;
       preserve valid Perl keywords, user functions, and prototype behavior
     - add CD and CHDIR for persistent directory changes; lowercase chdir
       retains ordinary Perl semantics
     - show exit instructions after Ctrl-C and use parenthesis-free function
       calls where appropriate in user examples and human QA/QC exercises
     - phrase uppercase hints as try, "COMMAND", avoiding Perl's use keyword
     - add explicit single-letter/digit shortcuts for all command operations
     - add immediate function/container shorthand and a bounded implicit-word
       list grammar; retain literal EVAL and normal Perl in stored source
     - confirm destructive shortcuts by default; ! explicitly bypasses the
       question, including shorthand redefinitions and file overwrites
     - restore direct E s/E a/E ar/E h/E hr and bare named-list shorthand;
       retain EVAL for literal Perl and native quote operators in list values
     - fix automatic completion of subroutine prototypes such as ($) and (@),
       which swallowed later commands; test human QA step 5 through terminal
       input in screen and plain modes, including CLS after a definition
     - install confirmation interrupt handling before displaying the prompt,
       so an immediate Ctrl-C cannot terminate the plain-input REPL
     - frame editable VRAM in white with two fixed command legend rows;
       reserve their space during wrapping, scrolling, resizing, and recovery
     - request blinking insert/overwrite cursors and restore the default on exit
     - print the requested farewell on interactive exit in screen and plain modes
     - cover Q/Q! and all full exit spellings in both terminal input modes;
       document how to identify an older loaded module when aliases are missing
     - compact the command legend to one line, giving 78x21 VRAM at 80x24
     - blink the cursor through timed visibility changes in the input loop,
       so blinking does not depend on the terminal honoring a style request
